    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-135315",
      "knowledge_point_id": "6eea26e0-2a9c-5d4c-91d3-12e7682e1858",
      "knowledge_point": "Inverting a Diagonal Matrix",
      "problem": "Find the inverse of the following matrix: \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Notice that the given matrix is diagonal.\n\nThe inverse of a diagonal matrix can be found as follows: \n\n$$\n{[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{11} & 0 & ⋯ & 0 \\\\ 0 & {a}_{22} & ⋯ & 0 \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋱ & ⋮ \\\\ 0 & 0 & ⋯ & {a}_{nn}\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{{a}_{11}} & 0 & ⋯ & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{{a}_{22}} & ⋯ & 0 \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋱ & ⋮ \\\\ 0 & 0 & ⋯ & \\frac{1}{{a}_{nn}}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nIn our case, we obtain\n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}={[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices_complete": true,
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}]",
              "option": "0",
              "source_option": "a"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}]",
              "option": "1",
              "source_option": "b"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}]",
              "option": "2",
              "source_option": "c"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}]",
