    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-135366",
      "knowledge_point_id": "6affd858-749d-5a94-854e-ddadd790ae45",
      "knowledge_point": "Inverting a Permutation Matrix",
      "problem": "Find the inverse of the following matrix:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "The given matrix can be obtained from the identity matrix by permuting its columns. Therefore, $A$ is a permutation matrix.\n\nThe inverse of a permutation matrix can be found as follows: \n\n$$\n{P}^{-1}={P}^{T}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1}={[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}={[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices_complete": true,
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]",
