      "worked_solution": "To find the domain of $f,$ we need the intersection of the domains of the individual components. \n\n- The domain of $\\sqrt{t+1}$ is $t\\in [-1,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of ${e}^{t}$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of $2t$ is  $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nThe intersection is illustrated in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14076578/assets/3f1ca1c3d6ffd56fe0686ee209c967775b5daf09a99e80a3f38ad0a56f4424ce.png)\n\nTherefore, the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)$ is $t\\in [-1,\\infty ).$",
