      "knowledge_point": "Domains of Functions With Exponential and Logarithmic Components",
      "problem": "Find the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)=\\sqrt{4-{t}^{2}}\\,i+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t-1)\\,j+{e}^{t}\\,k.$",
      "worked_solution": "To find the domain of $f$, we need the intersection of the domains of the individual components.\n\n- The domain of the 1st component $\\sqrt{4-{t}^{2}}$ is $t\\in [-2,2].$\n\n- The domain of the 2nd component $\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t-1)$ is $t\\in (1,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of the 3rd component ${e}^{t}$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nThe intersection is illustrated in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14076578/assets/d43c856bf43fb3783a7ee34b2553879fdb99a791587f1c1e466bc135c868052d.png)\n\nTherefore, the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)$ is $t\\in (1,2].$",
